# Cerberus system user for the vsock-watch detective control (installed to
# /usr/lib/sysusers.d/cerberus-vsock-watch.conf; systemd-sysusers creates the
# user/group via pacman's hook on install/upgrade). A DIFFERENT account than
# cerberus-api's "cerberus" user — see docs/vsock-connect-detection.md §4.3.
# Home is "-" (sysusers.d's no-home default) rather than /etc/cerberus: that
# directory belongs to the cerberus account, and two service accounts sharing a
# home undercuts the very isolation this account exists for.
#Type Name           ID GECOS                                     Home          Shell
u     cerberus-audit -  "Cerberus VSOCK-watch detective control" - /usr/bin/nologin
